  "source": {
    "system": "pasted",
    "id": "DIP-I-496",
    "title": "Show role and permission for a logged-in user",
    "body": "As a logged-in user I want to see which permission group I belong to, so that I know what I am allowed to do in the catalog and where to read the guidelines for it. Today the group is only visible to an administrator, in the Users table in Administration. Group names are set when the group is created and are often technical keys, so the group needs a separate readable name that an administrator can set. Note that a user can hold more than one group, and that a group can grant access in one catalog and not in another."
  },
